  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1217 AM CST Thu Nov 26 2026\n\nToday through Wednesday night...The rain has mostly ended across \nthe area tonight, but some drizzle and mist continue across the \narea. Drier air will build in across the area today and skies will\nbegin to clear over much of the area, but expect clouds to \npersist over the northeast. As cold air advection continues,\ntemperatures will remain cool, ranging from the mid 40s across the\nGolden Triangle to the mid 50s in northeast Louisianan. \nTemperatures tonight will fall just below freezing across most of \nthe area. The surface ridge will shift east of the area on Friday \nand the flow will become more southeasterly. Highs will mostly be \nin the mid 50s. \n\nSoutherly flow will increase out ahead over another front/short \nwave on Saturday with warmer highs in the upper 60s. The \nboundary will sweep across the area on Sunday, but it looks like \nmoisture/instability will be limited. Expect mostly scattered \nshowers/storms Sunday afternoon into the evening hours. High \npressure will build across the area on Monday and continue through\nthe end of the period./15/",
